WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.120
Finish your bisque and put away 
your snake, you kinky bastards,

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.740
because it's episode 3 of "American Horror Story",

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.640
and I think I just shit my pants.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.460
The episode begins with hot Satan
 finishing his interviews to determine

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.020
who is worthy of being admitted to Sanctuary.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.740
He says he's responsible for 
the seeds which will save mankind

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.140
and tells Gallant, Timmy and 
Mallory that they will be saved.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.980
Gallant feels sorry for killing his Nana, but 
Langdon tells him she died peacefully in her sleep.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.040
Then again, you can never 
really trust the spawn of Satan.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.600
He tells them that he has a 
power called "Night Vision of the Soul",

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.780
in which he can look into the 
places people want to keep hidden.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.480
Mallory, looking more and more like a 
kid from Whoville, is also interviewed by Langdon,

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.920
even though she's a Gray.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.280
Langdon can sense she wants to slit 
Coco's throat for how she's been treated by her.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.840
He's also surprised to see Dinah Stevens 
there. Apparently, they have a history.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.920
She says she's not powerful enough 
to stop whatever it is he has planned.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.660
Does he know that she is 
somehow related to the witches?

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.780
And if so, why would he want her to join Sanctuary?

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:05.700
He says,  "You're exactly the type of soul 
I'm looking for to build my new world."

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.780
He's not saving them. He needs their souls.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.600
We'll get into more of that in a bit.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:14.720
We learn that Andre is Dinah's son 
and that he thinks his mother is evil,

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:19.420
even though it was likely her who paid for 
him and his boyfriend for their Outpost tickets.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:25.540
Langdon tells Mallory that the rules of the old world, 
the rules that were honored in the breach, are over.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.420
This line, "the breach", is super interesting,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.520
because it hints at a war between 
the forces of Hell and either angels or witches.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.620
But now since the world has been decimated,

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.960
new rules and new conflicts 
between those forces will surely arise.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.080
He tells her that he wants people that 
will not only taste from the forbidden fruit,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.320
but cut the fucking tree down.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.320
"Forbidden Fruit" being the name of this episode 
and a reference to the story of Adam and Eve,

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.840
the snake and apple imagery 
making it even more evident.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:00.140
Mallory tells Langdon that it feels like 
someone is inside her, wanting to claw its way out.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.300
She tries to leave when he stops her,

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:06.620
but she unleashes a power so fearsome
 that it jettisons him across the room.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.280
He retaliates by showing his true form: an old man.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:17.200
Perhaps some sort of demon, or even his father, Satan, manifesting itself through him for a brief moment.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:23.840
Mallory retaliates again, exploding the fireplace, igniting the room in a fireball, much to Langdon's surprise.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.780
This is the first time all season 
Langdon loses his composure.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:33.640
He no longer is his usual calm self, 
rather surprised at not having the answers.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:38.140
He asks her, "Who are you?", and 
judging by her look, she doesn't know either.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:44.140
Langdon performs a satanic ritual similar to the 
one Gallant saw him do in his dreams in episode 2.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.600
He asks for power from his father, 
who is likely the Lord of Hell, Satan.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:52.680
He tells him that he thought he 
destroyed them all, but one survived.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.120
We're led to believe he's talking about witches,

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.360
but by the end of the episode, 
we know many of them are still alive.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:02.680
And with him knowing Dinah was one 
of them, is Mallory something different?

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.520
Not a witch, but an angel?

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.260
She even says to Langdon, "I have no dark places."

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.740
An angel would be the most logical this season,

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.880
providing a great foil to the Satanism of 
Michael Langdon and the Cooperative.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.060
As he continues the ritual, the blood 
begins to boil and snakes emerge.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.940
Looks like they didn't come from the pipes or 
ventilation shafts like Mead guessed in episode 2.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:29.820
Something takes over Langdon, his eyes turn 
jetblack and he says the words "Ave Satanas",

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.140
which is Latin for "Hail Satan".

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.220
In a series of kick-ass flashbacks,

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:40.860
we follow young Mead on Halloween,
 dressed coincidentally like a robot.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.700
At her first stop, she's given - 
guess what - a forbidden fruit.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:48.440
Fast forward to her first date 
watching "Rosemary's Baby",

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:51.220
a movie about a pregnant 
woman giving birth to the devil.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.020
There's even a dude wearing devil horns in the back.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:57.280
Fast forward again to her 
first kill as an agent for Mossad,

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:00.380
the International Intelligence Agency for Israel.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.517
Halloween seems to bring back her memories,

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.620
and if we remember from the 
dates on the emails in episode 2,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.700
Halloween is just around the corner.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.840
We find Mead is talking to Venable, 
letting her know about her being a robot,

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.060
questioning if all of her 
memories were simply programmed.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.520
She recollects one memory in particular 
of taking care of a little blond boy,

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.200
but the memory is such a blur.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:24.820
Is she referring to young Michael Langdon
 from season one's "Murder House"?

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.920
Venable tells her Langdon can't be 
trusted to take the right people to Sanctuary,

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.340
and when Mead finds out Venable 
wasn't chosen to go, they concoct a plan:

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.340
Kill them all, steal his computer, 
and find out where Sanctuary is.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:42.700
We're finally going topside, where the pus- and blister-filled cannibals are having a beach party.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:46.320
And look who it is from 
episode 1: Coco's boyfriend Brock.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:49.360
But something tells me she's 
not going to approve of his makeover.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:53.500
He asks them if they've heard of a bunker for the 
rich, when he's ambushed and fights them off,

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.520
his shotgun making quick work of them.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.940
A carriage similar to the one 
Langdon came in in episode 1 rushes away.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:04.100
But it can't be Langdon, since his 
horses were eaten at the end of that episode.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.360
It must be from someone else in the Cooperative.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.620
An alarm goes off, alerting 
Venable of a perimeter breach.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.220
It's the carriage, and inside is a box.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:15.760
But underneath Brock hides, 
using the carriage like a Trojan horse.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.960
In the decontamination chamber, the box is 
checked for radioactivity and is deemed clean.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.920
Inside are dozens of  apples.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:28.220
Venable thinks Langdon sent them to prove to the survivors what will be waiting for them in Sanctuary.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:33.440
She orders the Fist to take care of the horses while Mead offers a solution to their Langdon problem:

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:36.820
Hold a party and offer the poisoned apples as a gift,

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:41.140
killing every last person in 
Outpost 3 before taking care of Langdon.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.680
Remember, it was when Eve ate from the forbidden fruit

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.720
that she and Adam were banished from 
the Garden of Eden and lost eternal life.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.820
Topside, Brock stabs the Fist, stealing 
her key card to gain access to the Outpost.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:56.180
Mallory stares at the fire, questioning who she really is

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:00.120
as dissonant violin chords play, 
similar to those found in the shining.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:05.320
Venable calls an emergency meeting to announce 
their Victorian ball-themed Halloween party.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:09.080
With all they've been through,
they deserve a time to relax and let loose.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:14.400
Gallant does Coco's hair in what has to be one of 
the most outrageous hairstyles I've ever seen,

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:18.900
when Mallory asked if she can use Coco's 
Loubs - Louis Vuitton's - to make a mask.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.700
And if you know Coco, you know that ain't a go-go.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:25.220
She thinks the party's where they'll 
announce who gets chosen for Sanctuary,

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:28.040
and no way in hell is Mallory going to get chosen.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.860
Mallory tells them how she made 
the fire explode in Langdon's office.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:37.520
Kind of like the Dark Phoenix, a reference to the "X-Men"- character Jean Grey, who has telekinetic powers.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.060
Coco berates Mallory, telling her to prove it.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.320
"Uh, there's a fire right there, bitch."

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:44.560
But Mallory can't seem to harness her power.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:49.520
The party has begun and Mead brings in the 
forbidden fruit, so that everyone can bob for apples.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.720
A nod to season 1 and Zachary Quinto's character,

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.100
who prepared bobbing for apples on 
Halloween in the Murder House.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:59.340
Venable explains the importance of All Hallows' Eve,

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:02.360
when the boundary between 
this world and the other thins.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.780
Coincidentally, also the time when the boundary 
between the Outpost and the outside world thins.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:10.600
Bonus points if you saw Timmy's vest with the patches.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:16.420
Coco dances with who she thinks is Langdon, explaining how marvelous it will be when she's taken to Sanctuary.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:20.720
As a gesture of goodwill, she offers to give 
him something she never gave her boyfriend.

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:23.820
"I'm talking about anilingus."

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:28.280
She brings him back to her room and sorry, 
we don't get to see his radioactive penis.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:33.500
Brock reveals himself and Coco feigns 
happiness, saying how she's so glad to see him again.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:36.320
But he's not having it and stabs her in the face.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:41.780
Mead can't seem to find Coco or the Fist anywhere 
and suggests to Venable that they stop their plan.

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:43.400
There's too many witnesses.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:48.180
Venable says they must go forward, and we learn 
they used the snake venom to concoct their poison.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:51.220
She makes a toast to good fortune and everyone eats

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:55.100
before we're treated to the 
American Horror Story-equivalent of the Red Wedding.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:08:00.040
The denizens of Outpost 3 convulse,
vomiting up blood and bits of apple

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.520
'til every last one of them is dead.
Worst. Party. Ever.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:08.680
Venable and Mead inspect the dead, reveling 
in their victory before heading off to Langdon.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.940
At gunpoint, they tell Langdon 
they are making the selections now.

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:15.540
And in a cruel twist of malice,
 Langdon tells her that she passed.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.460
She'll be accepted to Sanctuary.

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:21.040
She instructs Mead to shoot, but 
Mead suddenly turns the gun and ...

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:23.100
Venable is killed.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.880
Mead's been under Langdon's control the whole time.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:29.440
Not only that, he was the one who 
came up with the poisoned apple plan.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:33.140
We learn she was made by the 
Cooperative Research and Development Department.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:36.460
A prototype of a woman who 
took care of Langdon as a child.

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:39.820
Langdon is the blond-haired boy 
she referenced earlier in the episode.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:41.500
But who is she modelled on?

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:46.640
The prevailing theory at the moment is she's based off Jessica Lange's character Constance from season 1,

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:49.660
the woman we see here 
taking care of young Michael Langdon.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:54.100
Then we're treated to the best part of 
the series so far: The return of the witches.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.640
Cordelia Goode, Myrtle Snow 
and Madison Montgomery.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:02.420
Cordelia breathes life into what she calls
their "sisters": Coco, Mallory and Dinah,

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.220
resurrecting them before Madison tells Mallory:

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:09.440
"Surprise, bitch. I bet you thought 
you'd seen the last of me."

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.620
But the question remains: How 
does Madison know Mallory?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.240
And is it connected to that thing 
inside her, clawing to get out?

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.080
Is it Zoe from season 3?

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:22.780
Potentially alluding to the spirits of Misty and 
Queenie in the bodies of Coco and Dinah?

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:24.800
Or is it something else entirely?

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:29.380
Madison isn't referring to Mallory 
herself but the thing inside her, the angel.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:35.380
Notice also how Mallory took off her glasses after being resurrected, seemingly curing her vision problems.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:40.400
If you recall from season 3 after Madison was resurrected, it cured her of her heart murmur.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.020
And what will happen to the others?

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.480
Surely, this isn't the last we'll see of Gallant.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:49.360
My guess is that since this was all part of 
Michael's plan, he now has access to their souls.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.940
So, we shouldn't count out that 
he'll be doing some resurrecting of his own.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:55.700
But this also calls into question the other bunkers.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.380
Were they overrun, like Langdon and Venable said?

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:00.300
Or were their souls taken by him?

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.960
If the bunker they're in used to be an all-boys school,

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.120
it's possible the Cooperative is tied to the 
warlocks, male practitioners of evil magic.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.980
This would provide a foil to the 
all-girls witches' coven in season 3.

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:17.620
So, are we looking at a battle between witches and the powers of Hell, or that of angels and demons?

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.940
Perhaps some combination of both.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:22.580
We'll just have to tune in next week to find out.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.440
Hey everyone, I hope you liked this video.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:29.940
As always, I hope you'll like, subscribe, share 
all that fun stuff and check out my other videos.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:31.180
And don't forget:

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.740
Daddy loves you very much.

